  "method": "Ten most recent successful runs per workflow across branches, plus the antimatter-vps runs of a job the runner gate may place there. Successful jobs only; elapsed time from first executed step start to last executed step completion, excluding runner queue time. Matrix variants and runners averaged independently; a job's budget is the largest, because the pick is made per run and the budget must cover whichever runner it gets. max(5, ceil(mean_seconds * 1.5 / 60)). Failed, cancelled and skipped jobs never increase budgets, with one reviewed exception recorded here: a job killed at its budget while every one of its steps had already concluded success (run 44308179842, test and lint on antimatter-vps-linux-x64) is not a hang -- its elapsed time is a floor for that runner, and the budget is the formula applied to it. Reusable timeout verified in the called workflow at its exact SHA; a reusable workflow in this repository is verified in place, at the commit the caller lands on.",
